cropmanager.guide.crop_sticks.title=IC2 Crop Sticks
cropmanager.guide.crop_sticks.desc=Place crop sticks on farmland and use a supported seed or IC2 Seed Bag on them.
cropmanager.guide.crop_sticks.info=Place a second set of sticks on empty sticks to prepare a crossing site. Grow mature parent crops nearby and keep the site clear of weeds.
cropmanager.guide.cropnalyzer.title=IC2 Cropnalyzer
cropmanager.guide.cropnalyzer.desc=IC2's portable analyzer reveals information about Seed Bags as their scan level increases.
cropmanager.guide.cropnalyzer.info=Charge it before use. It is an ingredient in the Seed Analyzer, which automates scans up to level 4.
cropmanager.guide.cropmatron.title=IC2 Crop-Matron
cropmanager.guide.cropmatron.desc=Supplies nearby IC2 crops with water, fertilizer and Weed-Ex.
cropmanager.guide.cropmatron.info=Give it EU and supplies. Link it to an Agricultural Monitor with the Agricultural Probe, or use it to craft an Advanced Crop Manager.
cropmanager.guide.crop_harvester.title=IC2 Crop Harvester
cropmanager.guide.crop_harvester.desc=Harvests mature IC2 crops and stores the produce.
cropmanager.guide.crop_harvester.info=Give it EU and keep the output clear. It is an ingredient in the Advanced Crop Manager.
cropmanager.guide.agricultural_probe.title=Agricultural Probe
cropmanager.guide.agricultural_probe.desc=Right-click IC2 crops to inspect growth stage, light, water, nutrients and catalyst charges. Species appears at scan level 1 and genes at level 4.
cropmanager.guide.agricultural_probe.info=Sneak-right-click an Advanced Crop Manager, Biogas Weeder or Crop-Matron to store its location. Right-click the Agricultural Monitor to link that target.
cropmanager.guide.seed_analyzer.title=Seed Analyzer
cropmanager.guide.seed_analyzer.desc=Give this tier 1 machine EU and an IC2 Seed Bag. It returns a fully analyzed bag and displays the crop's genetics and attributes.
cropmanager.guide.seed_analyzer.info=At default settings, one scan takes 100 ticks at 5 EU/t. Use the extract-only output for automation.
cropmanager.guide.radioactive_soil.title=Radioactive Soil
cropmanager.guide.radioactive_soil.desc=Place this block as subsoil beneath the farmland used for Radbloom. The crop sticks go on top of the farmland.
cropmanager.guide.radioactive_soil.info=Radbloom also needs light level 9 or higher and Catalytic Fertilizer to grow past stage 2. Mature plants can irradiate nearby entities. Wear a complete IC2 Hazmat suit.
cropmanager.guide.greenhouse_glass.title=Greenhouse Glass
cropmanager.guide.greenhouse_glass.desc=Place one block directly above an immature IC2 crop. The light level one block above the glass must be at least 9.
cropmanager.guide.greenhouse_glass.info=Each random tick on the glass adds 20 growth points by default to the crop immediately underneath. Empty sticks, weeds and mature crops get no bonus. A complete greenhouse is optional.
cropmanager.guide.crop.grinbloom.title=Grinbloom
cropmanager.guide.crop.grinbloom.desc=Harvest this tier 4 crop at stage 4 for Grin Powder. Use the powder in the Grin Extractor or to craft Catalytic Fertilizer and Mutagenic Powder.
cropmanager.guide.crop.grinbloom.info=Grows on IC2 crop sticks at light level 9 or higher. It returns to stage 2 after harvest.
cropmanager.guide.crop.bioreed.title=Bioreed
cropmanager.guide.crop.bioreed.desc=Harvest this tier 3 crop at stage 4 for Bio-Fiber. You can plant Bio-Fiber directly on IC2 crop sticks to start Bioreed.
cropmanager.guide.crop.bioreed.info=Needs light level 9 or higher and returns to stage 2 after harvest. Compost the fiber or craft it into IC2 Plant Balls.
cropmanager.guide.crop.nitrobulb.title=Nitrobulb
cropmanager.guide.crop.nitrobulb.desc=Harvest this tier 4 crop at stage 4 for Nitro Essence, an ingredient in Catalytic Fertilizer and Mutagenic Powder.
cropmanager.guide.crop.nitrobulb.info=Grows on IC2 crop sticks at light level 9 or higher. It returns to stage 2 after harvest.
cropmanager.guide.crop.lazuli_bloom.title=Lazuli Bloom
cropmanager.guide.crop.lazuli_bloom.desc=Harvest this tier 5 crop at stage 4 for a Small Pile of Lapis Lazuli Dust.
cropmanager.guide.crop.lazuli_bloom.info=Needs light level 9 or higher and a catalyst charge to grow past stage 2. Apply Catalytic Fertilizer to the sticks. Each harvest spends one charge and returns the crop to stage 2.
cropmanager.guide.crop.irid_moss.title=Irid Moss
cropmanager.guide.crop.irid_moss.desc=Harvest this tier 8 crop at stage 4 for an Iridium Shard.
cropmanager.guide.crop.irid_moss.info=Needs light level 9 or higher and a catalyst charge to grow past stage 2. Apply Catalytic Fertilizer to the sticks. Each harvest spends one charge and returns the crop to stage 2.
cropmanager.guide.crop.radbloom.title=Radbloom
cropmanager.guide.crop.radbloom.desc=Harvest this tier 7 crop at stage 4 for a Small Pile of Uranium-238. Place Radioactive Soil beneath the farmland and provide light level 9 or higher.
cropmanager.guide.crop.radbloom.info=Apply Catalytic Fertilizer to grow past stage 2. Each harvest uses one charge and returns the crop to stage 2. Mature plants emit light and can irradiate nearby entities. Wear a complete IC2 Hazmat suit.
cropmanager.guide.crop.glowbloom.title=Glowbloom
cropmanager.guide.crop.glowbloom.desc=Harvest this tier 4 crop at stage 4 for Glowstone Dust. It emits light level 6 at stage 3 and light level 12 when mature.
cropmanager.guide.crop.glowbloom.info=Grows on IC2 crop sticks at light level 9 or higher. It returns to stage 2 after harvest.
cropmanager.guide.crop.quartzreed.title=Quartzreed
cropmanager.guide.crop.quartzreed.desc=Harvest this tier 5 crop at stage 4 for Nether Quartz.
cropmanager.guide.crop.quartzreed.info=Needs light level 9 or higher and a catalyst charge to grow past stage 2. Apply Catalytic Fertilizer to the sticks. Each harvest spends one charge and returns the crop to stage 2.
cropmanager.guide.crop.lithivine.title=Lithivine
cropmanager.guide.crop.lithivine.desc=Harvest this tier 6 crop at stage 4 for a Small Pile of Lithium Dust.
cropmanager.guide.crop.lithivine.info=Needs light level 9 or higher and a catalyst charge to grow past stage 2. Apply Catalytic Fertilizer to the sticks. Each harvest spends one charge and returns the crop to stage 2.
cropmanager.guide.crop.sulfurbud.title=Sulfurbud
cropmanager.guide.crop.sulfurbud.desc=Harvest this tier 4 crop at stage 4 for a Small Pile of Sulfur Dust.
cropmanager.guide.crop.sulfurbud.info=Grows on IC2 crop sticks at light level 9 or higher. It returns to stage 2 after harvest.
cropmanager.guide.crop.resincane.title=Resincane
cropmanager.guide.crop.resincane.desc=Harvest this tier 4 crop at stage 4 for Sticky Resin.
cropmanager.guide.crop.resincane.info=Grows on IC2 crop sticks at light level 9 or higher. It returns to stage 2 after harvest.
cropmanager.guide.crop.cryolotus.title=Cryolotus
cropmanager.guide.crop.cryolotus.desc=Harvest this tier 3 crop at stage 4 for Snowballs.
cropmanager.guide.crop.cryolotus.info=Grows on IC2 crop sticks at light level 9 or higher. It returns to stage 2 after harvest.
cropmanager.guide.crop.cupric_moss.title=Cupric Moss
cropmanager.guide.crop.cupric_moss.desc=Harvest this tier 5 crop at stage 4 for a Tiny Pile of Copper Dust. Requires a Copper Block (ore:blockCopper) beneath the farmland.
cropmanager.guide.crop.cupric_moss.info=Needs light level 9 or higher, a Copper Block subsoil, and a catalyst charge to grow past stage 2. Apply Catalytic Fertilizer to the sticks. Each harvest spends one charge and returns the crop to stage 2.
cropmanager.guide.crop.stannum_herb.title=Stannum Herb
cropmanager.guide.crop.stannum_herb.desc=Harvest this tier 5 crop at stage 4 for a Tiny Pile of Tin Dust. Requires a Tin Block (ore:blockTin) beneath the farmland.
cropmanager.guide.crop.stannum_herb.info=Needs light level 9 or higher, a Tin Block subsoil, and a catalyst charge to grow past stage 2. Apply Catalytic Fertilizer to the sticks. Each harvest spends one charge and returns the crop to stage 2.
cropmanager.guide.crop.voltreed.title=Voltreed
cropmanager.guide.crop.voltreed.desc=Harvest this tier 6 crop at stage 4 for Redstone. Requires a Block of Redstone beneath the farmland.
cropmanager.guide.crop.voltreed.info=Needs light level 9 or higher, a Block of Redstone subsoil, and a catalyst charge to grow past stage 2. Apply Catalytic Fertilizer to the sticks. Each harvest spends one charge and returns the crop to stage 2.
cropmanager.guide.advanced_crop_manager.title=Advanced Crop Manager
cropmanager.guide.advanced_crop_manager.desc=Supply this tier 2 machine with EU, water, Weed-Ex and fertilizer. It tends IC2 crops and can automatically harvest them into its output.
cropmanager.guide.advanced_crop_manager.info=Use the area tab to set the scan radius and vertical layers. The data tab summarizes crops and conditions after a full scan. Configure genetic filters and redstone behavior in the GUI.
cropmanager.guide.agricultural_monitor.title=Agricultural Monitor
cropmanager.guide.agricultural_monitor.desc=Use an Agricultural Probe to link a farm machine in the same dimension. The Monitor displays its status and can send it compatible supplies.
cropmanager.guide.agricultural_monitor.info=Configure automation thresholds and redstone alerts in the GUI. Optional upgrades extend the default 32-block range, move harvests, or supply wireless EU.
cropmanager.guide.biogas_weeder.title=Biogas Weeder
cropmanager.guide.biogas_weeder.desc=Fill with IC2 biogas and set the scan area. It removes actual weeds from crop sticks and stores the IC2 Weed item in its output.
cropmanager.guide.biogas_weeder.info=It runs on biogas alone and leaves weeds in place when the output is full. Empty the output and use the Weed in a composter.
cropmanager.guide.electric_composter.title=Electric Composter
cropmanager.guide.electric_composter.desc=Supply tier 1 EU, water and compostable items. By default it turns 4 organic items and 1,000 mB of water into 1 IC2 Fertilizer.
cropmanager.guide.electric_composter.info=The default cycle takes 200 ticks at 5 EU/t. The machine accepts IC2 upgrades and an electric battery.
cropmanager.guide.thermal_pipe.title=Thermal Pipe
cropmanager.guide.thermal_pipe.desc=Connect an IC2 heat source to a compatible machine. The pipe carries heat along connected sections.
cropmanager.guide.thermal_pipe.info=The default throughput is up to 100 HU/t.
cropmanager.guide.manual_composter.title=Manual Composter
cropmanager.guide.manual_composter.desc=Right-click with compostable material. Sneak-right-click to fill faster. Fermentation starts automatically when the composter reaches capacity.
cropmanager.guide.manual_composter.info=By default, 8 inputs make 2 Organic Compost. Add a water bucket or water bottle to double the speed. Right-click when ready to collect.
cropmanager.guide.organic_compost.title=Organic Compost
cropmanager.guide.organic_compost.desc=Collect it from a Manual Composter. Apply it directly to IC2 crop sticks to replenish nutrients and hydration.
cropmanager.guide.organic_compost.info=It also works in the Advanced Crop Manager and is an ingredient in Catalytic Fertilizer, Radioactive Soil and the Agricultural Manual.
cropmanager.guide.catalytic_fertilizer.title=Catalytic Fertilizer
cropmanager.guide.catalytic_fertilizer.desc=Use on IC2 crop sticks or supply it to an Advanced Crop Manager. It restores nutrients, adds growth points to immature plants and refreshes catalyst charges.
cropmanager.guide.catalytic_fertilizer.info=Catalyzed crops need a charge to progress past stage 2. Harvesting one spends a charge. Inspect remaining charges with the Agricultural Probe.
cropmanager.guide.mutagenic_powder.title=Mutagenic Powder
cropmanager.guide.mutagenic_powder.desc=Use on empty double crop sticks near mature parents to advance IC2 crossing attempts and suppress weeds. A successful cross can gain a small stat bonus.
cropmanager.guide.mutagenic_powder.info=Load it into a Pollinator Hive to speed up nearby breeding pulses. Raise and compare the resulting crops before choosing the next parents.
cropmanager.guide.pollinator_hive.title=Pollinator Hive
cropmanager.guide.pollinator_hive.desc=Place it near double crop sticks prepared for crossing. It advances one eligible site per pulse in a default 5 × 5 × 3 area.
cropmanager.guide.pollinator_hive.info=Right-click with Mutagenic Powder to charge it. It pulses three times as fast while charged and spends a charge on a successful pulse. It also runs uncharged.
cropmanager.guide.grinding_blade.title=Grinding Blade
cropmanager.guide.grinding_blade.desc=Insert a blade in the Grin Grinder to process spider eyes into Grin Powder.
cropmanager.guide.grinding_blade.info=The blade wears on completed cycles and lasts 256 uses by default. Replace it when worn out.
cropmanager.guide.grin_grinder.title=Grin Grinder
cropmanager.guide.grin_grinder.desc=Supply tier 1 EU, spider eyes and a Grinding Blade. Each completed cycle produces one Grin Powder and wears the blade.
cropmanager.guide.grin_grinder.info=The default cycle takes 100 ticks at 5 EU/t. Use the powder in the Grin Extractor or in fertilizer recipes.
cropmanager.guide.grin_extractor.title=Grin Extractor
cropmanager.guide.grin_extractor.desc=Supply tier 1 EU, Grin Powder and water. The default cycle turns 1 powder and 1,000 mB of water into 1,000 mB of Grin Extract.
cropmanager.guide.grin_extractor.info=The default cycle takes 100 ticks at 5 EU/t. Send the extract to the Weed-Ex Mixer.
cropmanager.guide.weed_ex_fabricator.title=Weed-Ex Mixer
cropmanager.guide.weed_ex_fabricator.desc=Supply tier 1 EU, redstone and Grin Extract. The default cycle turns 1 redstone and 1,000 mB of extract into 500 mB of Weed-Ex.
cropmanager.guide.weed_ex_fabricator.info=The default cycle takes 100 ticks at 5 EU/t. Use fluid pipes or containers to supply farming machines.
cropmanager.guide.nitro_essence.title=Nitro Essence
cropmanager.guide.nitro_essence.desc=Harvest Nitrobulb at stage 4 to obtain this agricultural ingredient.
cropmanager.guide.nitro_essence.info=Use it in the crafting recipes for Catalytic Fertilizer and Mutagenic Powder.
cropmanager.guide.bio_fiber.title=Bio-Fiber
cropmanager.guide.bio_fiber.desc=Harvest mature Bioreed for Bio-Fiber. Plant the fiber on IC2 crop sticks to grow another Bioreed.
cropmanager.guide.bio_fiber.info=Both composters accept it. You can also arrange four fibers in a square to craft an IC2 Plant Ball.
cropmanager.guide.sprinkler_mk1.title=Sprinkler Mk1
cropmanager.guide.sprinkler_mk1.desc=Hydrates farmland and IC2 crops in a default 9 × 9 area across its own level and one level above and below.
cropmanager.guide.sprinkler_mk1.info=Place it over a water source for continuous operation or refill its 4,000 mB tank by bucket or pipe. It also adds growth points to immature IC2 crops.
cropmanager.guide.sprinkler_mk2.title=Sprinkler Mk2
cropmanager.guide.sprinkler_mk2.desc=Covers a default 9 × 9 area across three vertical levels. It pulses four times as often and gives four times the growth points per pulse as Mk1 by default.
cropmanager.guide.sprinkler_mk2.info=Place it over a water source or fill its 8,000 mB tank by bucket or pipe.
cropmanager.guide.sprinkler_mk3.title=Sprinkler Mk3
cropmanager.guide.sprinkler_mk3.desc=Covers a default 17 × 17 area across three vertical levels with the same pulse speed and growth bonus as Mk2.
cropmanager.guide.sprinkler_mk3.info=Place it over a water source or fill its 16,000 mB tank by bucket or pipe.
cropmanager.guide.agricultural_reservoir.title=Agricultural Reservoir
cropmanager.guide.agricultural_reservoir.desc=Build a tower 3 × 3 and 5 blocks tall. Use 41 casings for the solid floor, roof and walls. Leave the middle layers hollow. Place the outward-facing controller at the center of a side wall in a middle layer.
cropmanager.guide.agricultural_reservoir.info=Right-click the controller. The two tanks start at 32,000 mB each. Copy a filter from a filled container, configure ports by face, and connect tier 1 EU for automatic fluid delivery at 1 EU per 50 mB.
cropmanager.guide.reservoir_casing.title=Reservoir Casing
cropmanager.guide.reservoir_casing.desc=Use casings for the solid roof, solid floor and side walls of the Agricultural Reservoir.
cropmanager.guide.reservoir_casing.info=Leave the middle of each interior layer empty and replace one middle-layer wall position with the controller. Use the reservoir interface to configure exterior fluid ports.
cropmanager.guide.reservoir_capacity.title=Capacity Expansion
cropmanager.guide.reservoir_capacity.desc=Install it in the capacity slot of a formed Agricultural Reservoir or Industrial Fluid Reservoir.
cropmanager.guide.reservoir_capacity.info=Adds +16,000 mB per tank (up to 4) in the Agricultural Reservoir, or +32,000 mB (up to 8, reaching 384,000 mB) in the Industrial Fluid Reservoir.
cropmanager.guide.reservoir_pump.title=Reinforced Pump
cropmanager.guide.reservoir_pump.desc=Install this module to double the Agricultural Reservoir's automatic transfer rate.
cropmanager.guide.reservoir_pump.info=Enable automatic delivery on the tank and supply EU to the controller. The transfer costs 1 EU per 50 mB.
cropmanager.guide.reservoir_reserve.title=Reserve Valve
cropmanager.guide.reservoir_reserve.desc=Install this module to retain a minimum amount of fluid in each Agricultural Reservoir tank.
cropmanager.guide.reservoir_reserve.info=Set each tank's reserve in the controller. The available settings are 0, 25, 50 and 75 percent of that tank's capacity.
cropmanager.guide.weed_killer_upgrade.title=Weed Killer Upgrade
cropmanager.guide.weed_killer_upgrade.desc=Install in the Advanced Crop Manager to clear actual IC2 weeds as it scans.
cropmanager.guide.weed_killer_upgrade.info=Keep the machine supplied with EU and Weed-Ex. It uses 20 mB of Weed-Ex per removal at default settings.
cropmanager.guide.wireless_range_upgrade.title=Wireless Range Upgrade
cropmanager.guide.wireless_range_upgrade.desc=Insert this upgrade in an Agricultural Monitor to double its wireless link range.
cropmanager.guide.wireless_range_upgrade.info=With defaults, the range starts at 32 blocks and reaches 512 with four upgrades. Keep the linked machine in the same dimension.
cropmanager.guide.wireless_eu_upgrade.title=Wireless EU Upgrade
cropmanager.guide.wireless_eu_upgrade.desc=Sneak-right-click an IC2 energy storage block to bind the upgrade. Install it in a compatible IC2 machine to draw EU from that storage in the same dimension.
cropmanager.guide.wireless_eu_upgrade.info=In the Agricultural Monitor, upgrades let it receive EU and wirelessly power its linked equipment and nearby compatible Agronomy Expansion machines.
cropmanager.guide.harvest_transfer_upgrade.title=Harvest Transfer Upgrade
cropmanager.guide.harvest_transfer_upgrade.desc=Install it in an Agricultural Monitor linked to an Advanced Crop Manager.
cropmanager.guide.harvest_transfer_upgrade.info=The Monitor pulls harvested items into its internal buffer. Extract them from the Monitor with compatible pipes or hoppers.
cropmanager.guide.upgrade_linker.title=Upgrade Linker
cropmanager.guide.upgrade_linker.desc=Sneak-right-click a placed Crop Database Chest with the Linker to bind it to that chest.
cropmanager.guide.upgrade_linker.info=Craft the bound Linker with a Portable Crop Database, or hold the Portable in your other hand and right-click with the Linker. The link applies to the Portable and the Linker is consumed in survival.
cropmanager.guide.agricultural_manual.title=Agricultural Manual
cropmanager.guide.agricultural_manual.desc=Right-click to open this guide. Browse its categories or search for a crop, machine or item.
cropmanager.guide.agricultural_manual.info=Craft a book with either Organic Compost or Reservoir Casing. Both recipes work in any arrangement.
cropmanager.guide.crop_database_chest.title=Crop Database Chest
cropmanager.guide.crop_database_chest.desc=Stores 500 IC2 Seed Bags in pages of 25. Search, sort, and mark individual bags as favorites with middle-click or Shift+R while hovering over a bag.
cropmanager.guide.crop_database_chest.info=Enable nearby collection or deposit bags from your inventory through Settings. The recipe requires a fully charged Lapotron Crystal and separate IC2 Universal Fluid Cells holding water and Weed-Ex.
cropmanager.guide.portable_crop_database.title=Portable Crop Database
cropmanager.guide.portable_crop_database.desc=Carries 500 IC2 Seed Bags and supports automatic pickup when enabled. Its crafting recipe requires an unused Crop Database Chest and a fully charged Energy Crystal.
cropmanager.guide.portable_crop_database.info=Sneak-right-click a placed Crop Database Chest with the Portable to link it, or use a bound Upgrade Linker. A linked Portable opens the chest across dimensions while its chunk is loaded. Link it again to change the target.
